      "question": "What happens if I close a credit card with a balance?",
      "answer": "Closing a credit card does not eliminate the debt you have incurred, and you still owe the remaining balance to the card issuer. The CFPB publication does not outline specific reporting timelines or point changes for closed cards carrying balances. Ask the card issuer how the closed account will be reported."
